  (descr "A copper disc fed by a short strip above a small ground plane: the classic printed UWB antenna. It covers the whole UWB band at 50 ohm, without a balun (S11 below -10 dB from about 2.6 to 11 GHz). The disc radius R sets the lowest frequency; the feed gap G and the ground length GL set the match in the middle of the band. Keep the ground small and the gap narrow: a longer ground or a wider gap makes the match worse.")
